  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance to the Transfer of Ukrainians to Long Term Accommodation in Ireland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to the implementation of the temporary protection directive with a focus on supporting long term accommodation for Ukrainians and third country nationals (TCNs) having entered Ireland since 24 February 2022. The project will facilitate the safe and orderly movement and transportation facility of Ukrainians and TCNs to their long-term accommodation and manage an effective tracking system. This will include the provision of movement support to Ukrainian nationals and TCNs, from their current short-term accommodation in Ireland to the long-term solutions.  It will also support Ukrainian nationals and TCNs to be supported with their immediate needs when settling into a new house and assist in pre departure group orientation from the hotel and vulnerability screening when required for onward referral to relevant local institutions as regards their protection and security needs.</narrative>
  </description>
